# Database and security

- `supabase/migrations/` is the source of truth for schema, functions, triggers, grants, and RLS.
- Add a **new timestamped** migration (`YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_name.sql`) after the latest file. Never rewrite an applied migration.
- Default all work to local Supabase. Do not `db push`, `link`, or mutate a remote project without explicit authorization (hook will ask).
- Do not hand-edit `src/lib/database.types.ts`. Regenerate with `scripts/gen-types.sh`.

## Security invariants

- RLS is **default-deny**. Enable RLS before or with the table. Add explicit policies; never rely on table grants alone.
- Public reads: published posts, visible comments, public catalogs (tags, projects, timeline, site_settings, media metadata). Drafts, revisions, and pending comments stay owner-only (authors may see their own pending comments).
- `SECURITY DEFINER` functions must set `search_path` (empty or an explicit list). Validate auth inside the function. Use `(select public.is_owner())` / `(select auth.uid())` so Postgres can initplan.
- GRANTs are explicit. Anon is select-only on public catalogs. No client `INSERT` on `profiles` (trigger-only). Revoke leftover `PUBLIC` execute on definer functions, then grant the minimum roles.
- Service-role clients bypass RLS. App code must not use `src/lib/supabase/admin.ts`. Owner bootstrap is `scripts/grant-owner.mjs` only.
- Never log or expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`.

## Verification

- After migration changes: `supabase db reset` locally, then `pnpm test:integration` when `.env.test` exists.
- Delegate `blog-db-reviewer` for RLS, grants, definer functions, or privileged clients.
